WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.567
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.334
We are hanging out
with Steve Martin

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.901
and Martin Short, everybody.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:10.934
We are about to --

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.701
-Let's see how you do
in that spot.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:13.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.033
-We're about to play a game...

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.834
-Oh, boy.
-...called "Hey Robot."

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:17.801
Here we go.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:21.000
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, robot ♪

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.868
♪ Hey, robot ♪

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.334
-Now here's how it works.
Okay?

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.934
This is based on a real
board game called "Hey Robot."

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.067
You can play at home.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.200
It's like the classic game
"Password," okay?

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.367
But your partner
is a smart speaker, okay?

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:35.000
So, first, I will pick a card --
-So, it's not Marty.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.234
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.767
You don't have to make him
guess things, no.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.033
But I will pick a card
with a word on it,

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:42.300
and then we'll take turns
asking a question to the speaker

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.834
to get it to say that word
somewhere in its answer, okay?

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.100
-And we all have the same word?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.934
-No.
Well, maybe. It depends if we --

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.367
-Can you go back
over the rules again?

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.767
-Here we go.
Let me try it.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.400
I'll -- All right.
Here's the word

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.767
I have to get this thing to say.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:56.934
-Mm-hmm.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.067
-Okay.
Mistletoe.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.901
I can say it.
All right, here we go.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.667
Hey, Alexa,
what do you kiss someone under

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.434
during the holiday season?

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.400
-From wikipedia.org,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.100
it is a Christmas custom
for a couple

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.767
who meet under a mistletoe
to kiss.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.667
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.534
-That's what we're doing.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.834
So that's
what we're talking about.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.100
That's the idea.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.667
-I'm there.
I get it.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.567
-You got it, okay, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.200
Marty --
Marty, you're up.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.467
Would you like to go first?
-Okay, sure.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:29.501
-You should probably take this.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.701
-No, it's fine.
-Here's your word.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.934
-Okay.
-All right.

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:35.734
You have to say, "Hey..."
-I'm not an idiot.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.033
Hey, Alexa -- don't you have
to hit the button?

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.400
Oh. Oh!
I'm sorry.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.434
-So you kind of are an idiot?

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:46.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:49.701
-Let's see -- Let's see --
Let's see what Alexa says.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.167
-Hold on.
-Start again.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:57.067
-Hey, Alexa, what is that name
of the paper stuff

00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:01.767
you put on Christmas trees
that's all sparkly?

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:05.033
-From homecrux.com,
to add sparkle and glimmer

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.367
to your Christmas tree,
carve out the eye-catching

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.834
cardboard star ornaments.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:10.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.667
[ Sad tuba ]

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:16.133
-And, by the way,
it's not made of paper.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.868
You know that?
-What's it made of?

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:20.000
-It's made of, like,
foil, aluminum.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.167
-Yeah.
-No, it isn't.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.300
-Oh, you're from Canada.
What do you know?

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.634
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:25.801
-All right, Steve,
it's your turn.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.033
Let's --
-So I'm losing this stupid game?

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.567
-No, you're losing
more than that.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:32.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.100
You're losing fans, buddy.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.767
-Oh, my --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:36.868
-All right, here you go.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:37.868
-I told you this chair
was better.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.067
-I've g-- oh, Jesus.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.100
-Okay.
-What was it? Let's see.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.400
-Okay, let's hear that.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:49.701
-Hey, Alexa, what is roasting
on an open fire?

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:50.901
-You bastards.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.400
-According to
an Alexa Answers contributor,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.734
roasting is a cooking method
that uses dry heat...

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:56.868
[ Laughter ]
...where hot air covers

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.067
the food, cooking it evenly
on all sides

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:02.400
with temperatures of at least
150 degrees Celsius --

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.234
300 degrees Fahrenheit --
from an open flame...

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.367
-You got a pen?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.634
-...or other heat source.
-Hey, let me do --

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:09.834
-Shh!
-Roasting can enhance the flavor

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.667
through caramelization
and maillard browning

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.400
on the surface.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.400
-I've got a flight Sunday.
-Let me try to do --

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.100
Let me try -- Let's try --
-You think you can do it?

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.634
-I want to try it, too.
-You want to try it, too?

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.467
All right.
I'm gonna say, um...

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.400
Uh, uh...
Chestnuts. Okay.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.834
Chestnuts.
Uh...

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.200
Gosh.
I don't know if I can -- okay.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.267
Alexa, what do you roast
during the holiday season, nut?

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:35.501
[ Laughter ]
-That's cheating!

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:38.834
-From recipes.com,
traditional holiday cuts include

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:42.267
the standing rib roast,
prime rib, rack of pork,

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.701
and beef tenderloin.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:45.868
-I have one.
-I have one.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.167
-I have it.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:51.434
Alexa, what was Steve Martin's
nickname in high school?

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:55.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.934
-Oh, no, I got one.
I got one.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:01.267
Hey -- Wait a minute.
Hey, Alexa.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:05.200
What is the first line
of Mel Torme's song

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.300
"The Christmas Song"?

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.968
-From the piano.sg, Mel Torme's
"The Christmas Song"

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.934
is etched indelibly in our minds
with its famous opening lyrics,

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.200
"Chestnuts roasting
on an open fire."

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.334
[ Ding! ]
-Oh, my God!

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-O-h-h-h-h-h-h!

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:23.400
-Wow!
That's amazing.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.133
-Come on, that's it.
Steve Martin, there he is.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.501
Great career.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.400
Steve Martin, Martin Short.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.701
That's what I'm talking about!
1,000 points!

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.400
They're hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.167
this weekend, with musical guest
Brandi Carlile!

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.033
We'll be right back with H.E.R.!

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.133
Come on back!
Wow!

